review_text:
Racist restaurant, suggest to avoid, shame on Rosewood branding. The staff (at least one of the staff named Erica) was obviously poorly trained and was very rude and impolite and even discriminating her customer.

My friend was feeling unwell and vomited after the wine, we asked Erica politely to please bring us some tissue. And here is how we were treated in a restaurant within a FIVE star hotel:

1. She shouted immediately “Oh Shit” in front of us;
2. Without showing any care or support, she requested us to clean the table and throw everything (including the tableware) on the table by ourselves to the trash bin (there is no trash bin nearby), otherwise we will be fined by the restaurant;
3. We asked her to please bring us a plastic bag/paper bag so that we can clean the table, she rejected (more than one time) and said they don’t have any plastic/paper bags. Instead, she said you can do it with the tissue?! However her colleague and herself later brought us the plastic/paper bags;
4. She kept repeating for at least five times that we have to clean the table and throw the glass on the table by ourselves otherwise we will be fined;
5. Her attitude through the process was rude, impolite, totally unprofessional and made me feel like being discriminated.

Overall it was an extremely bad experience where we are not being treated as a customer or even a proper human being.
